Z||000000||moneypimp||08-08-2001||02:58 PM||||My 86SE 2.8 auto trans just developed a problem.  At normal acceleration the trans shifts fine but at wide open with the pedal to the floor the trans down shifts for passing then won't shift to a higher gear unless you back of the pedal.  I tried adjusting the TV cable but no change.  What goes here?  Does anyone have a suggestion???||||reg||1
Z||000001||Joe Torma||08-08-2001||03:20 PM||||Sounds like your kick down cable is still out of adjustment. Probably from slamming your foot to the floor too much   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Try pulling it out another notch.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 08-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||08-08-2001||07:34 PM||||There may be an internal problem. If it was working then stopped, it's likely there's dirt in someplace it shouldn't be. Could actually be a bad part. There are a bunch of GM TSB's on the TH125. One of them may help if you can find them.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 08-08-2001).]||||reg||1
